## The template

```js
function backtrack(state) {
  if (isComplete(state)) { record(state); return; }

  for (const choice of choices(state)) {
    if (!isValid(choice, state)) continue;   // prune early

    apply(choice, state);      // choose
    backtrack(state);          // explore
    undo(choice, state);       // un-choose
  }
}
```

Every backtracking problem is this shape: N-Queens, Sudoku, word search, combination sum, generate parentheses, palindrome partitioning.

**Pruning is what makes it tractable.** Without `isValid`, N-Queens explores 8⁶⁴ positions; with it, a few thousand.

