## Handling duplicates

```js
nums.sort((a, b) => a - b);
// inside the loop:
if (i > start && nums[i] === nums[i - 1]) continue;   // skip duplicate branches
```

Sort first so duplicates are adjacent, then skip repeats at the same recursion depth. This is the standard trick and it appears in every "II" variant of these problems.

