## Coin change — fewest coins for an amount

```js
function coinChange(coins, amount) {
  // dp[i] = fewest coins to make amount i
  const dp = new Array(amount + 1).fill(Infinity);
  dp[0] = 0;                                  // base case: 0 coins for 0

  for (let value = 1; value <= amount; value++) {
    for (const coin of coins) {
      if (coin <= value) {
        dp[value] = Math.min(dp[value], dp[value - coin] + 1);
      }
    }
  }

  return dp[amount] === Infinity ? -1 : dp[amount];
}

coinChange([1, 5, 10, 25], 63);   // 6  → 25+25+10+1+1+1
```

**Time O(amount × coins), space O(amount).**

The recurrence: `dp[v] = min over coins of dp[v - coin] + 1`. "The best way to make 63 is one coin plus the best way to make 63 minus that coin."

---

## Greedy fails here

```text
coins = [1, 3, 4], amount = 6
Greedy: 4 + 1 + 1 = 3 coins
Optimal: 3 + 3   = 2 coins
```

Greedy works for standard currency systems because they are designed to, but not in general. Being able to produce that counterexample is a strong answer.

