## Top-down memoisation

Often easier to derive — write the recursion, then add a cache:

```js
function coinChange(coins, amount, memo = new Map()) {
  if (amount === 0) return 0;
  if (amount < 0) return Infinity;
  if (memo.has(amount)) return memo.get(amount);

  let best = Infinity;
  for (const coin of coins) {
    best = Math.min(best, coinChange(coins, amount - coin, memo) + 1);
  }

  memo.set(amount, best);
  return best;
}
```

| | Top-down | Bottom-up |
|---|----------|-----------|
| Easier to write | ✅ mirrors the recursion | Needs the fill order |
| Computes only what is needed | ✅ | Fills everything |
| Stack overflow risk | ✅ deep recursion | No |
| Space optimisable | Harder | ✅ often O(1) |

