## Objects need a key

```js
const users = [{ id: 1, name: 'Ada' }, { id: 1, name: 'Ada' }];

[...new Set(users)].length;    // 2 — different object references!
```

```js
// ✅ Deduplicate by a key — last occurrence wins
function uniqueBy(items, keyFn) {
  return [...new Map(items.map((item) => [keyFn(item), item])).values()];
}

uniqueBy(users, (u) => u.id);   // one user
```

The `Map` constructor takes entry pairs and later keys overwrite earlier ones — which is exactly deduplication. To keep the **first** occurrence instead, reverse before and after, or use an explicit loop with a `has` check.

