## The caveats worth stating

Big O hides constants, and constants matter at real sizes. An O(n²) algorithm with a tiny constant can beat O(n log n) for n = 50 — which is why V8's sort switches to insertion sort for small arrays.

And in frontend work, the dominant cost is usually **DOM nodes and network latency**, not algorithmic complexity. Knowing which one you are actually bound by is more valuable than the notation itself.

## The naive version and its cost

```js
