## Step 2 — a trie for prefix search

When you need prefix matching over tens of thousands of entries:

```js
class Trie {
  constructor() { this.root = { children: new Map(), items: [] }; }

  insert(word, item) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word.toLowerCase()) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) {
        node.children.set(char, { children: new Map(), items: [] });
      }
      node = node.children.get(char);
      if (node.items.length < 50) node.items.push(item);   // cap per node
    }
  }

  search(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix.toLowerCase()) {
      node = node.children.get(char);
      if (!node) return [];
    }
    return node.items;
  }
}
```

**Search is O(m)** where m is the query length — completely independent of dataset size. Building costs O(total characters) once.

Capping `items` per node bounds memory; without it, the root node holds every item.

