## Longest palindromic substring

Expand around each possible centre. There are 2n-1 centres, because a palindrome can be odd or even length:

```js
function longestPalindrome(s) {
  let best = '';

  function expand(left, right) {
    while (left >= 0 && right < s.length && s[left] === s[right]) {
      left--; right++;
    }
    return s.slice(left + 1, right);
  }

  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    const odd = expand(i, i);         // centre on a character
    const even = expand(i, i + 1);    // centre between characters
    best = [odd, even, best].sort((a, b) => b.length - a.length)[0];
  }

  return best;
}
```

**O(n²)**. Forgetting the even-length centres is the standard bug.

