## Approach 2 — min-heap of size k

Keep the k largest seen so far; the root is the kth largest.

```js
function findKthLargest(nums, k) {
  const heap = new MinHeap();

  for (const num of nums) {
    heap.push(num);
    if (heap.size > k) heap.pop();   // evict the smallest — keeps the top k
  }

  return heap.peek();                // smallest of the top k = kth largest
}
```

**O(n log k) time, O(k) space.** For k = 10 out of a million elements, substantially better than sorting.

JavaScript has no built-in heap, so you would implement a binary heap or use a library — mention that explicitly.

