## The parallel-execution follow-up

> "How would you run independent tasks concurrently?"

Everything at the same *level* — same in-degree-zero batch — can run in parallel. Process level by level rather than one task at a time:

```js
while (queue.length) {
  const batch = [...queue];       // this whole level is independent
  queue.length = 0;
  await Promise.all(batch.map(run));
  // decrement in-degrees, enqueue newly unblocked tasks
}
```

That is precisely how Turborepo parallelises a monorepo build.
